%LCAsami
%LC麻实
\dA-Are you trying to imply that I'm dirty?!\d%K%P
「你、你是说我和脏兮兮的样子很配？\n这个意思吗！？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dDon't be silly. Toko's only looking at it from a\npractical perspective.\d%K%P
「完全不是啊。\n都子只是往实用性方面讲而已」%K%P
As long as we had the freedom of a positive\ninterpretation.%K%P
稍微往好的方面解释了。%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dI mean, didn't you rent your dress last time, too? I\nheard you went to Karuizawa's church with a rental car\nright after graduation, and got married with only your\nfriends attending the ceremony.\d%K%P
「再说了，之前的礼服也是租借的吧？\n听说老师毕业那天用租凭车去了轻井泽的教堂，\n只是邀请了朋友」%K%P
%LCAsami
%LC麻实
\dHow much did you tell her?!\d%K%P
「你都说到哪去了！？」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dThere are no secrets between me and Osamu! Right?\d%K%P
「我和理君之间可没有任何隐藏的事情哦\n是吧～理君？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dEh? Ah, um... I suppose... so...?\d%K%P
「啊？啊，不…嘛…那个…」%K%P
That being the truth only made it harder for me to react.%K%P
虽说那是不争的事实，但说出来也太恶趣味了…%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dYou didn't care much about it in the past, but now you're\ngoing out of your way to send out invitations and\neverything.\d%K%P
「明明以前那种奔放的事都做过了。\n现在却怎么又为了宾客的座位顺序而如此小题大做呢」%K%P
%LCAsami
%LC麻实
\dUm... after spending a few years in society as adults,\nyou end up tangled up in all sorts of responsibilities you\ncan't ignore.\d%K%P
「我说啊…\n我到底是步入社会好几年了，\n各种无法无视的事情也增加了啊」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dWhich reminds me, Vice Chief Hiragi said he didn't want\nall the responsibilities that came with being the main\nspeaker.\d%K%P
「提到邀请函，我倒是想起来了…\n平木副部长，都事到如今了，他突然闹着说不要做证婚人了」%K%P
%LCAsami
%LC麻实
\dEh?! But we can't change it now!\d%K%P
「啊！？\n怎么会，到现在突然要换是不可能的！」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dLook... could you stop destroying the image I had of\nmarriage...?\d%K%P
「所以呀，不要把我对婚姻的幻想夺走啊…」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dWell, the last time we spoke, he kind of broke out into\ntears, begging me not to drag him to the center of the\nstage ever again, so...\d%K%P
「但是他说『别再把我扯到表舞台上了』，\n在我面前哭起来了…」%K%P
Even I was taken aback.\nHad he been dealing with more stress at work lately?%K%P
即使是我也会多少有点退缩…\n他最近，到底积了多少压力啊。%K%P
%LCAsami
%LC麻实
\dNo way... But where could we find someone to replace\nhim...? Your president declined without hesitation, so...\nhow about Vice President Yoshitomi...?\d%K%P
「怎么会…事到如今了，能代替他的人…\n社长早就拒绝了，吉富副社长…？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dIf we put him in that position, we'll be kicked out by\nthe next arriving couple by the time he's done with the\ntoast.\d%K%P
「如果让他担任，等他说完的时候，\n恐怕就到下一对的婚宴了…」%K%P
%LCAsami
%LC麻实
\dBut then... we're only left with one option...\d%K%P
「那就没有剩下的候补了…」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dWhy not ex-Managing Director Sawashima?\nI thought she was Osamu's direct superior.\d%K%P
「不是还有嘛，泽嶋原董事。\n不就是理君的直属上司吗？」%K%P
%LCAsami
%LC麻实
\dDon't even joke about that!\d%K%P
「别开玩笑啦！？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dDon't take her seriously, Asami. Besides, tradition\ndictates to have a married couple as the main speakers.\d%K%P
「别当真啊麻实…\n证婚人本来就必须是已婚人士」%K%P
It didn't seem like the whole mother and daughter-in-law\nrelationship in our family was showing much progress. If\nanything, I felt like we were sinking deeper and deeper\ninto a swamp.%K%P
那之后，婆媳问题一点解决的征兆都没看到，\n反倒是在沼泽里越陷越深了…%K%P
But this problem illustrated the situation I was dealing\nwith quite aptly.%K%P
倒不如说，正因为这些问题的爆发，\n我现在也必须说明情况就是了。%K%P
...%K%P
………%K%P
Our ceremony was being planned for next spring.%K%P
婚礼在明年春天举行。%K%P
I'd be thirty by that time, with Asami being only two\nyears younger than me. And so, we concluded that going for\na somewhat extravagant ceremony wouldn't be too bad.%K%P
迈入三十岁的我，和仅仅比我小两岁的麻实，\n抱着『传统的婚礼也不错』这种想法，\n也能冷静地得出这种圆滑的成人结论了。%K%P
We received various comments, such as how we shouldn't be\nso proud of getting married a second time, but none of it\nbothered us. Perhaps it was a sign of us getting older.%K%P
既然能对周围的『第二次可不能如此规规矩矩地举行』\n之类的杂言碎语完全置若罔闻，\n看来我们也渐渐变成大叔大妈了也说不定。%K%P
After all... when it came down to it, our own happiness\nmeant the most to us.%K%P
即便如此，嘛…\n彼此都能幸福的话，那就没有什么比这更令人开心的了。%K%P
Solving our main problem was still at an infantile stage,\nbut we were slowly and surely moving forward with our\nsearch for an answer.%K%P
我们的问题在于向着解决的方向努力，\n现在好歹会有一个可喜可贺的开始。%K%P
